 <LayoutMultiFrame templateUuid="{7e568462-4542-48df-baad-f0c3d76656ea}" evaluateExpressions="true" url="" resizeMode="0" stylesheet="body { margin: 33.3333 33.3333;line-height: 122%;color: rgba(0,0,0,1.0000);font-family: Noto Sans, ;font-style: normal;font-weight: 400;font-size: 14.6991px;text-align: center; }" type="65648" contentMode="1" html="&lt;p>The Geospatial Enabling Environments for Employment Tool (GeoE3), developed by the &lt;strong>World Bank&lt;/strong>, evaluates locations based on how supportive they are of employment and business opportunities.&lt;/p>&#xa;&#xa;&lt;p>By incorporating 15 spatial factors across three dimensions:&lt;/p>&#xa;&#xa;&lt;ol>&#xa;    &lt;li>&lt;strong>Contextual&lt;/strong>&lt;/li>&#xa;    &lt;li>&lt;strong>Accessibility&lt;/strong>&lt;/li>&#xa;    &lt;li>&lt;strong>Place Characterization&lt;/strong>&lt;/li>&#xa;&lt;/ol>&#xa;&#xa;&lt;p>GeoE3 offers a comprehensive analysis of how the environment impacts job prospects, indicating whether it is highly enabling or not enabling at all.&lt;/p>&#xa;&#xa;&lt;p>This plugin is built with support from the &lt;strong>Canada Clean Energy and Forest Climate Facility (CCEFCF)&lt;/strong>, the &lt;strong>Geospatial Operational Support Team (GOST, DECSC)&lt;/strong> for the project Geospatial Assessment of Employment and Business Opportunities in the Renewable Energy Sector. This project is open source; you can download the code at &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/worldbank/GEOE3&quot;>https://github.com/worldbank/GEOE3&lt;/a>.&lt;/p>&#xa;&#xa;&lt;p> &lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p> &lt;/p>&#xa;&#xa;&lt;p>Developed by &lt;a href=&quot;https://kartoza.com&quot;>Kartoza&lt;/a> for and with the WorldBank.&lt;/p>" uuid="{7e568462-4542-48df-baad-f0c3d76656ea}" maxBreakDistance="10" useSmartBreaks="true" stylesheetEnabled="true">
  <childFrame templateUuid="{e507bfbc-fb82-414d-b2bf-bca9c49f4208}" uuid="{e507bfbc-fb82-414d-b2bf-bca9c49f4208}"/>
  <LayoutObject>
